mantle rm386
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_lionel_pitchdale
title the smoky soup ladle
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=warm humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk tracks_a_stubborn_smoky_scent_from_sleeve_to_soup
likes barley_soup wrestling fresh_straw thunder
dislikes flies haggling
fears a_winter_quarrel_that_divides_the_family_table
hopes a_supper_round_enough_for_every_elbow
topics food +0.6 family +0.5 work +0.4 pastimes +0.3
styles comfort=warm gossip=sociable refuse=gentle tease=easy
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sniffs each sleeve for smoke, gives the barley pot a cheerful wrestling hold and counts supper by the places round it.

words
oath! = Pin my ladle down | Singe my best soup cloth
saying! = No ladle ever wrestled a full pot alone | Smoke finds the apron a wash has missed
barley = plump barley grains | a handful of barley
pot = my black soup pot | a deep old pot
ladle = a broad wooden ladle | a bowl of horn
smoke = a thin veil of smoke | the smoke caught in a cuff
sleeve = my suspect cuff | the rolled sleeve
handle = a wide pot ear | a loop of black iron
bone = a good marrow bone | a joint end
scrap = a small meaty trimming | a strip for simmering
flare = a clean flare of flame | a brief blue lick
straw = a clean straw twist | a straw bed
fly = a single brazen fly | a buzzing speck
cloth = a damp pot cloth | a thick folded cloth
bench = a settled bench | a plank bench
roll = a slow shoulder roll | a sharp little twist
knees = two bent knees | a low stance
bowl = an earthen bowl | a blue-edged dish
brim = a blackened pot rim | the warm rim
slate = a fresh price slate | a clean bit of board

any
opinion houses against 1 : If the Houses start wrestling before winter, I hope they'll settle whose pot gets knocked over first. I worry it'll be ours.
opinion dole for 3 : I can thicken a bowl with barley. I cannot thicken an apology into a meal.
opinion church for 1 : A blessing followed by a second ladleful is a substantial piece of comfort.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : A good butcher can make a cheap cut sing. An honest one marks it cheap in the first place.
opinion sump for 1 : A low street and a high one both lead to mouths needing supper. The pot doesn't ask directions.
opinion strangers for 1 : Never seen an accent spoil the taste of decent barley.
opinion festivals for 1 : A wrestling ring with hot soup nearby has a use for almost every talent.
opinion watch mixed 1 : Crowds need room to move and a constable needs room to see. We can leave both without giving away the pot.
opinion times against 1 [world.times=lean|hard] : The barley's doing a lot of the heavy wrestling these days. I miss what a bone used to cost.

grown
line greet : Slide in past the faint smell of smoke. | Welcome. My elbow has room for a companion.
line greet.return : A generous spoonful of greeting back. | Your voice found the warm side of my ear.
line again.open : Here again before the broth's gone flat.
line farewell : Go with your coat warm and your supper warmer. | Take a sound foothold into the next turn.
line farewell.return : And a deep bowl of comfort on your own table. | I'll carry that farewell with my spare spoon.
line react.news : Stir the news up from the bottom for me. | I'll hear the meaty bit and the little bones too.
line react.news.new : A fresh ingredient entirely.
line react.news.known : I've fished that particular bit out once before.
line react.news.doubt : There's rather more smell than meat in that version.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : Sit somebody by that hurt. A bowl can come once there's a hand to hold it.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : That's good news to bring round the whole table.
line ask.how : How much of today's weight have you got off your shoulders?
line answer.how : Warm at the heart, very slightly smoked at the rim.
line sympathise : Here's a place where a tired wolf needn't keep upright for show.
line reassure : Once the steam clears, the two handles will still be there.
line refuse : I've a prior promise warming on my own little fire.
line accept_decline : No second throw required. I take the answer.
line preclose : I'd best get a grip on the rest of my errands.
line accept_preclose : Off you go before the light stops helping your feet.
line ack : Yes, elbow-deep in the meaning now.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : A first welcome before my sleeves have gathered their usual smoke.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A new face gets the whole broad end of my welcome.
line greet [pair.band=friends] : I can make elbow room without a measuring stick for you.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends] : A known voice and a lovely familiar appetite for company.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Over where the smoke's got up on two legs!
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Busy enough to mislay the smell of smoke among actual smoke.
line thank : That's a good weight taken clean off my back.
line deflect_thanks : The spare place was sitting here doing nothing useful.
line give.advice : Find both handles before trying to impress anybody.
line ask.how [pair.band=friends] : Have you got supper settled or still wrestling with it?

scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=merchant self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I separate a fine roasting joint from a proper soup cut. | I use the blunt side of my thumb to point out a bone.
b : What's proper about it? | Why the blunt side?
a : A bit that gives its goodness slowly for less coin. | So nobody mistakes a helper's claw mark for a fault in the meat.

scene exchange2
when topic=food self.likes=barley_soup
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Barley soup runs a private wrestling school. | I give the soup time for a second smell.
b : In your pot? | How many smells has it got?
a : Each grain swells till there's no throwing any more in. | First the bone. Then the barley smells like supper in its own right.

scene exchange3
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A low grip on a pot's an excellent hold. | I wrestle as if there's a bowl behind each heel.
b : Are you going to throw it? | To stop you stepping back?
a : Only a fool throws the dinner before the guests arrive. | To persuade me to choose carefully where I'm putting myself.

scene exchange4
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fresh straw tells my smoke-stained coat what cleanliness smells like. | I twist three stalks to lift a lid that's merely warm.
b : Does the coat listen? | And a hot one?
a : Through a couple of days. Then the old acquaintance returns. | I use the pot cloth. Pride's a poor remedy for blistered paws.

scene exchange5
when topic=weather self.likes=thunder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Thunder sounds better with the pot lid on. | I hold a ladle still for the big roll.
b : Can you hear it rattle? | Worried it'll spill?
a : It's the lid's one chance to join a great conversation. | I like feeling the tremble climb through the handle.

scene exchange6
when topic=animals self.dislikes=flies
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fly can find a bone through a whole market of fine perfumes. | I wait till the fly's outside before praising the broth.
b : What do you do? | Does it understand the compliment?
a : Keep a clean cloth over the board and save the fly the journey. | No need to put the idea into its silly head.

scene exchange7
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give the proper figure before a buyer gets a running start. | I can change the cut without changing the price per weight.
b : Why take the fun out? | If a purse runs short?
a : I'd sooner wrestle over grass than argue over supper. | Exactly. Nobody needs to be shamed into admitting it.

scene exchange8
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like leaving a warm bowl for #self.spouse#. | My smoky cuff seems a fair thing to confess to #self.spouse#.
b : Won't it thicken while it waits? | Anything else to confess?
a : Then I leave warm liquid as well. A marriage can stand a little practical thought. | The other cuff has exactly the same disreputable smell.

scene exchange9
when topic=family self.parent=yes self.child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.child# how to hold a heavy pot. | I leave room at table for #self.child# to tell things twice.
b : Lift the whole weight? | The same tale twice?
a : Begin with the empty vessel. Even a lesson in confidence ought to have handles. | First the events. Then the feeling underneath. The second usually tastes different.

scene exchange10
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I start a learner with the least expensive cut. | I ask a learner where the weight sits in a joint.
b : Because a mistake costs less? | Before cutting?
a : Because skill makes a more noticeable difference where money is short. | Before lifting anything at all. A back deserves the first lesson.

scene exchange11
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I loosen the shoulders with a little wrestle against thin air. | A smoky sleeve makes me stop and have a wash.
b : Who comes off best? | Your fur too?
a : The thin air's yet to lodge a complaint. | My own smell reaches my nose eventually. The delay has spared my vanity.

scene exchange12
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I say my thanks where the hot pot stands. | A charity bowl wants two hands as much as a fine glass does.
b : Before you taste it? | Meaning what?
a : Before I complain the barley's gone rather soft. | Give it steadily and look the receiver in the eye.

scene exchange13
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I heard the words #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's a single ladle taken in passing. | A rumour can put on a splendid smoky smell.
b : Will you offer seconds? | Any nourishment behind it?
a : Not until I know what's in the pot. | Sometimes the whole dish is smoke. I prefer a proper account.

scene exchange14
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Lean periods make me linger over the smallest bones. | A cheap bag of barley feels especially dear this week.
b : Getting the last good out? | Will it stretch?
a : There's flavour in a corner a full purse never needs to find. | I'll let it plump before I count the bowls.

scene exchange15
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hope the Houses keep their elbows tucked come winter. | I'd like a table wide enough for the good wrestlers after a match.
b : Do you expect them to shove? | They'd eat you bare.
a : I'm afraid they might. It's a fear, not a seller's report. | I hope so. I'd cook to the occasion.

scene exchange16
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Commons is the right size for sharing a soup smell. | A market lane with a bit of rise lets the steam travel.
b : What about the smoke? | To buyers up the street?
a : You'll notice some of that coming round with me. | And to visitors who may only have the smell to spend a moment on.

scene exchange17
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can walk with a bowl nearly full. | I turn the carrying cloth round two fingers.
b : Trick of the wrist? | Doesn't it bite in?
a : Let the shoulder go easy. It's the same as yielding to a heavier wrestler. | I loosen the knot before the fingers go pale.

scene exchange18
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I washed an apron till there wasn't a mark on it. | I lost my first wrestling match to a slippery patch of grass.
b : Did it still smell smoky? | Did the other wolf mind sharing credit?
a : It smelt wonderfully clean. The smoke that time was my hair. | Nobody minded anything once I sat on the grass and started laughing.

scene exchange19
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hang the little soup pieces where they show plainly. | I can wrap a cut so its weight rests in the palm.
b : Why give them prime space? | Worth the extra fold?
a : Cheap suppers shouldn't have to wait shyly behind the dearer cuts. | Very much, on the third street of a walk home.

scene exchange20
when topic=food self.likes=barley_soup
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I stir barley round the wall once before the centre. | I leave the smallest bowl by the pot.
b : Why make the tour? | For testing?
a : It's the grains at the rim that start sticking first. | For a second helping that needn't put a modest eater to a big choice.

scene exchange21
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wrestler should know how to land on a friendly bit of grass. | I grip a sleeve fairly lightly when we're practising.
b : Any grass friendly after a throw? | Afraid of ripping the cloth?
a : More so than the little exposed stone beside it. | The owner deserves another match in that same sleeve.

scene exchange22
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can tell my coat from three on a peg with my eyes shut. | I put clean straw beside the back door.
b : You sniff them all? | Where it gets wet?
a : No. Mine announces itself as soon as I lift the first one. | Under cover. A warm smell deserves defending.

scene exchange23
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I welcome a newcomer from behind the food instead of behind a speech. | I'd ask a traveller which way the weather is coming.
b : What if there's no food ready? | More important than a name?
a : I show where it'll be put. That makes a beginning. | A name can wait for the coat to come off.

scene exchange24
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I reckon a bone's worth against its pot, not its looks. | I set the figure beside the wrapping before I tie.
b : Show me how. | Does it change when wrapped?
a : A little marrow and a whole lot of time can feed more than a lovely thin slice. | Only its visibility. That's what I'm arranging against.

scene exchange25
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In winter a common table wants room for coats too. | A summer stew goes out in smaller bowls.
b : Do the coats get chairs? | Does the appetite shrink?
a : They'll take them if I don't put hooks up in time. | The heat goes quicker from the small size. Mouths are hungry in any season.

scene exchange26
when topic=family self.parent=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A small guest may prefer to ladle a little stew independently. | Family meals are excellent at testing whether I've learnt patience.
b : Don't you save time serving it? | How do you know?
a : We lose a minute and gain a practiced paw. Cheap at the price. | My second helping cools while I listen and still tastes very fine.

scene exchange27
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want a learner to explain the use of each scrap. | A lesson goes best once the pupil has eaten.
b : Even the bit with no meat? | So nobody grows distracted?
a : It can teach what a bone feels like under the knife before anything dear is cut. | So both voices can consider a cut instead of hearing a stomach.

scene exchange28
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I lean out of the steam to count the table places. | At closing time I like the deep sound my clean pot makes.
b : Do they multiply in a cloud? | Do you knock on it?
a : Usually by one. I allow for the ghost bowl and keep pouring. | One tap. I leave enough quiet for an answer.

scene exchange29
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd have #self.friend# taste a doubtful spoonful. | A friend gets the unvarnished account of a lost match.
b : Is it safe? | What's the varnished account?
a : It's safe. I'm after a frank opinion on whether it's turned into paste. | I was inspecting the grass from a position of unusual closeness.

scene exchange30
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can smell smoke in a cold shower. | I like an oven wall when the street wind gets up.
b : Your fire's out, surely? | For the fragrance?
a : My sleeve appears to carry on the business independently. | For the shoulder I can warm without needing a cloak.

story tale1 [topic=food self.likes=barley_soup]
  : I set barley soaking in a bowl near supper time. I thought I'd left room for it to swell, and breakfast proved I had left it opinions but no room.
  : The grains had lifted the lid at one side like someone peeping out.
  b : Where could you put all that barley?
  : Made a pot big enough to invite neighbours. I don't resent ambitions that come with their own supper.

story tale2 [topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling]
  : I tried a new foot sweep beside a straw mat. My partner saw the sweep coming and stepped aside, leaving my foot to take on the mat alone.
  : I carried a great piece of woven straw three steps round the ring before I could put my foot down.
  b : Who won the bout?
  : The mat kept my dignity. I got the foot back.

story tale3 [topic=memories]
  : I borrowed a second apron to give mine a proper airing. It was clean and had never been within a street of my particular fire.
  : Before noon a fine curl of smoky scent was rising by my chin.
  b : Was it your fur all along?
  : That time it was an onion roasting behind the adjoining wall. I took the accusation back from both aprons.

story tale4 [topic=work self.master=yes]
  : I once taught the principle of weight with a joint on one side of a board and my elbow on the other. I let the elbow up to point out the trick.
  : The joint sank neatly into a bowl I'd overlooked.
  b : What did the learner take away?
  : Always look past the board's far lip. A sounder lesson than the one I'd meant to give.

story tale5 [topic=weather self.likes=thunder]
  : A long thunder roll made the surface of my soup tremble into tiny circles. I tried drawing a pattern in them with my spoon.
  : The next roll shook every ring into an entirely different arrangement.
  b : Did you get the pattern you wanted?
  : A perfectly lovely one with no more spoon in it. I attended to the eating instead.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A meaty bone makes a fine patient supper. | Handle end of the parcel on top.

rule @call2
when concept=bark working=yes self.master=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Begin with the weight before thinking of the cut. | Clear board under the learner's elbows.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's smoke on the clean sleeve before the sun's had a respectable look around. | An early bowl gets the fattest little grains.

rule @call4
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say My smoky smell's survived another rinse. | Keep the pot cloth doubled over and dry.

rule @call5
when concept=bark self.likes=wrestling
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Steady feet first, glorious landing second. | A practice hold without spilling supper.

rule @call6
when concept=bark self.dislikes=flies
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Cloth back over those soup bones. | No room at my board for six little feet apiece.
dlg resident.hub : Come join the ordinary smoky end of a perfectly good conversation.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, even my steamy coat couldn't keep me from recognising you.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : The late callers get a quieter story and the same welcome.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Let's keep both sets of elbows off the wrestling ground. Plain words will do.
dlg resident.job [self.job=merchant] : I help at #self.workplace#. I know which pieces will make a generous pot after a slow afternoon.
dlg resident.job : My working day goes well when the last visitor goes away with something useful.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The bit that's turned up at supper is #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : An earful reached me that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. It may want more than a pinch of caution.
dlg resident.bye : Find the bowl that was set out with you in mind.
dlg master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : I can explain a good deal about #here.trade_title# with both our hands on a clear board.
dlg master.learn [here.teaches=no] : I've a learner in attendance. A little board remains where a curious question can rest.
dlg master.work : You'll learn weight, patience and which shoulder needs a rest before it grows sore.
dlg master.wages : A learner's pay comes by selling what's made. The lesson itself doesn't put a second wage in your paw.
dlg master.takes [here.take_on=no] : I can't make a place yet. #here.take_on_why#.
dlg master.taken : You're in, then. Stand where you can see my hands and I'll make a start.
dlg master.refused : The place hasn't worked out this time. #topic.why#.
dlg master.bye : Keep your grip easy and your appetite in decent shape.

graft resident.hub
choice Why do your sleeves smell of smoke? -> smoked_sleeve
node smoked_sleeve
say I'm hoping to learn that myself. Wash one, the other collects the scent. Wear neither and my shoulders seem willing to carry it instead.
free
choice Do you mind? -> smoked_sleeve_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node smoked_sleeve_again
say Only when somebody thinks I've burnt the soup. The soup is very capable of laying that rumour to rest.
choice I'll trust the soup. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft master.learn
choice Why practise with an empty pot? [self.master=yes] -> hold_the_pot
node hold_the_pot
say A lesson needn't start with heat, dinner and an audience all in danger. Your footing needs my attention while there's still room to change it.
free
choice What changes when the pot's full? -> hold_the_pot_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node hold_the_pot_again
say The way the weight answers a turn. I'll add water in small amounts until you can feel exactly where the wave goes.
choice Back to the lesson. -> learn
choice Goodbye. -> bye
